  "notes": "Def Jam / Roc-A-Fella teen soloist working mid-2000s Atlanta and NY 808 R&B, 2005–2010. The research gives \"65–104 straight/half-time mix\" and states the switch precisely — \"the clap on 3 below 80 BPM and on 2&4 above\" — so the straight half is encoded, 80–104 with `halfTime` false and the mode at 88, and the sub-80 half-time half is the other backbeat class. Three drum deltas: an 808 kick at two to four hits a bar with `lockTo808` at 0.55 and a 0.2 tresillo lean, a clap stacked flat on 2 and 4 on a dead-flat grid, and \"offbeat maraca, triplet fills\" — an offbeat shaker/conga/snap bed at three to five hits a bar plus a `16T`/`32T` hat roll vocabulary at 0.24 per bar. This is a true 808 model: \"808 sub with slides on the root, prominent, long decay\" is the whole low end, so `drums.bass808` carries role `bassline` and there is no `bassline` block. Harmony is \"single- or two-chord minor beds with a bell/plucked riff\", so the single-chord family shares top weight and the triad share is high. \"Light alto in a narrow band, chant hooks, doubled rather than stacked harmony\" is an eighteen-semitone melody register, a riff-dominant contour, a 3–5 pitch motif and a counter density of 0.3. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity, density and portamento number is INFERRED, and the 808-R&B grammar is sourced at tutorial level for the sub-lane rather than for this name. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode two-chord vamps [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry gives the one-chord and the two-chord bed equal billing — \"minor-mode two-chord vamps\" / \"single- or two-chord minor beds with a bell/plucked riff\" — and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\"), so a `vamp` weight of 6-of-8 made the two-chord half of that sentence almost unreachable. `vamp` keeps the top weight; the two-chord reading is now reachable at both rates. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
